  "narrative": {
    "intro": "South Carolina has received $9.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 18,503 awards, with an average award size of $516K, and obligations are up 14.6% year over year. The Department of Energy is the largest buyer in the state, having obligated $4.9B, followed by the Department of Defense with $2.6B. The top vendors include SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC at $3.4B and SAVANNAH RIVER MISSION COMPLETION, LLC at $1.1B. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry by obligations at $3.7B, and Remediation Services is the second at $1.1B. Recent fiscal years show fluctuations: FY23 had $10.1B, FY24 had $10.6B, and FY25 had $8.3B before the current FY26 total of $9.5B. These figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial. The distribution of spending is highly concentrated in a few large agencies and vendors, and the industries with the largest obligations reflect energy, environmental remediation, construction, and engineering work in the state.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal spending in South Carolina trended recently?",
        "body": "Obligations rose and fell across recent fiscal years: FY21 was $6.7B, FY22 was $7.2B, FY23 was $10.1B, FY24 was $10.6B, FY25 was $8.3B, and FY26 to date is $9.5B. The current fiscal year is showing obligations up 14.6% year over year. The number of awards in FY2026 to date is 18,503, with an average award size of $516K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy is the largest buyer, having obligated $4.9B, followed by the Department of Defense at $2.6B and the Department of Health and Human Services at $751M. SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC and SAVANNAH RIVER MISSION COMPLETION, LLC are the top vendors at $3.4B and $1.1B respectively, and Facilities Support Services and Remediation Services lead industries at $3.7B and $1.1B respectively."
      }
    ]
